    "q-349312": {
      "dom_id": "step-q349312",
      "name": "Question 18",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14187307/assets/ea20fd21d0d8924163615500ebf0c5aaa1823a68121c0fc574624dfd8182fbf6.png)\n\nA box contains $25$ colored pencils. The ratio of red pencils to blue pencils is shown in the diagram above. How many blue pencils are in the box?",
      "worked_solution": "The tape diagram shows $3$ boxes corresponding to red pencils, and $2$ boxes corresponding to blue pencils. Therefore, the ratio of red to blue pencils is $3:2.$\n\nWe are told that there are $25$ pencils in total. The tape diagram has $3+2=5$ boxes in total. Therefore, each box in the diagram above represents $25÷5=5$ pencils.\n\nNow, we fill the number $5$ in each box of both tapes:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14187307/assets/58a4e9ce8130b4e84307652c4237e0d898cfb56a9f25ab00669d376b3bfb4515.png)\n\nSince there are $2$ boxes corresponding to blue pencils, and each box represents $5$ pencils, the number of blue pencils must be:\n\n$$\n2\\times 5=10\n$$\n\nSo, there are $10$ blue pencils in the box.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
